        "date": "2026-11-24T04:26:57Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): start-side Arc entry plunges in air outside the stock box\n\nOn a 2D Offset pass that starts Inside or Outside round a part, the Arc\nentry of each level now plunges in air at least the tool radius plus the\napproach distance off the stock box. A straight lead in air, tangent to\nthe arc, then one G17 arc of Arc radius and Arc sweep run onto the first\nring. The lead is proved against the cutter-centre area joined with the\nair outside the box, and across no planned pass.\n\nWhere no air lead fits (Inside: the other rings enclose the first one),\nthe entry stands down to a named helix or ramp, or the op is refused by\nname. The axial dive and the vertical arc ramp into material are no\nlonger stand-ins. A re-entry after a lift tries the air entry and a\nclear helix before the named plunge; the four plunges that stay on fig8\nOutside are pinned known-fail on #3747.\n\nFixes #3746\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
